message: >-
  If you use these results, please cite the paper. Until it has an arXiv identifier,
  cite this repository and the release tag you used.
title: "Erdős Problem 357: Lean formalization, verification scripts and computations"
version: "1.1.0"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/dreadpiratechan/erdos-357"
url: "https://quanalabs.com"
authors:
  - family-names: Snively
    given-names: Chandler
    affiliation: Quana Labs
keywords:
  - Erdős problems
  - distinct consecutive sums
  - additive combinatorics
  - formal verification
  - Lean 4
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 formalization, verification scripts and computations for the paper
  "Bounds for increasing sequences with distinct consecutive sums (Erdős Problem 357)".
  It proves f(n) <= (44273/90000) n + 2 sqrt(n) + 177792 and f(n) >= (15/sqrt(21)) sqrt(n) - 1800
  for n >= 12096*504^2, where f(n) is the largest number of integers 1 <= a_1 < ... < a_k <= n
  with pairwise distinct consecutive sums. The results were produced with AI systems; see
  docs/PROVENANCE.md.
preferred-citation:
